  "_about": "How the analyser finds a language requirement in a posting (scripts/analyze.py, language_requirement). For each language: the words that name it ('anchors'), a few stop words so a posting's own language can be detected, and optional extra phrases. The generic phrases for levels (CEFR, 'native', 'fluent', 'very good', 'good') are shared by all languages and live under `phrases`. All text is matched after lower-casing and folding accents, so write terms without accents (ä -> ae, é -> e, ñ -> n).",
